// D16851: a maker with an annotated parameter returns a hole lambda capturing it, and its calls'
// values are delivered at two function types. Each call builds its own closure over its own
// argument, so the design owes both.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/README.md, "Template format".
// @@PRELUDE@@
function adder(n: f64) { return (a) => a + n }
// @@VALUE@@
adder(2)
// @@TYPE@@
(a: i32) => f64
// @@PROOF@@
print(v(3))
// @@WANT@@
5
// @@VALUE2@@
adder(2.25)
// @@TYPE2@@
(a: f64) => f64
// @@PROOF2@@
print(v(0.5))
// @@WANT2@@
2.75
